sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Mumbai as Mumbai desk<br/>(Taj Colaba)
  participant API as guest-score-api
  participant PG as PostgreSQL
  participant V as Verifier<br/>(UIDAI / passport office)
  actor Lisbon as Lisbon desk<br/>(never seen this guest)

  rect rgb(248, 250, 252)
    Note over Mumbai,PG: First contact — a file is opened on a domestic document
    Mumbai->>API: POST /api/identity/resolve<br/>{country: IN, type: aadhaar, number: ...}
    API->>API: Validate format + Verhoeff check digit locally
    Note right of API: A typo caught here costs nothing.<br/>Sent upstream it writes a near-miss<br/>identity number into somebody's log.
    API->>V: Verify with the issuing authority
    V-->>API: {status: "simulated"}<br/>no credentials configured
    API->>API: HMAC-SHA256(key, country‖type‖number)
    Note right of API: The number is never stored.<br/>Only the keyed hash and the last 4,<br/>which is what makes holding an<br/>Aadhaar-derived value defensible.
    API->>PG: INSERT guests + identity_documents<br/>(one transaction)
    PG-->>API: hash is unique → file opened
    API-->>Mumbai: GS-488122DBCBB0 · tier "New" · 500<br/>deposit 100% · portable: false
    Note over Mumbai: "This file has no portable document.<br/>Add the guest's passport before they travel."
  end

  rect rgb(248, 250, 252)
    Note over Mumbai,PG: The guest adds a passport — the file becomes portable
    Mumbai->>API: POST /api/guests/{id}/documents<br/>{country: IN, type: passport}
    API->>PG: INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (hash) DO NOTHING
    PG-->>API: 1 row → attached
    API-->>Mumbai: portable: true · notice cleared
  end

  Note over Mumbai,Lisbon: months later, a different country, a different member

  rect rgb(248, 250, 252)
    Note over Lisbon,PG: Resolution — the same standing follows the person
    Lisbon->>API: POST /api/identity/resolve<br/>{country: PT, type: passport, number: ...}
    API->>API: Same HMAC over the same document
    API->>PG: SELECT guest_id FROM identity_documents WHERE hash = $1
    PG-->>API: g_… → GS-488122DBCBB0
    API->>PG: INSERT INTO inquiries (append-only)
    Note right of PG: The guest is entitled to know<br/>who pulled their file. An inquiry<br/>never affects the score.
    API-->>Lisbon: matched: true · opened: false<br/>Rohan Mehta · the record from Mumbai
  end

  Note over Mumbai,Lisbon: Without the shared hash index, Lisbon opens a second file<br/>and a guest outruns a bad record by crossing a border.
